launcher_changes_needed:
provisioning/fleetres/fleetres.c - new verb 'FLEETRES.EXE -avpvideo <file> <w> <h>', mirroring avp.exe exactly:
(1) refuse w<512 or h<384;
(2) LoadLibraryA("ddraw.dll") and GetProcAddress "DirectDrawCreate" (no static ddraw import), then DirectDrawCreate(NULL,&dd,NULL). This is the primary display, which an all-zero GUID in AvP_Video.cfg selects;
(3) IDirectDraw_EnumDisplayModes(dd, 0, NULL, &ctx, cb) with dwFlags=0, as at avp.exe 0x559629. Collect dwWidth, dwHeight and ddpfPixelFormat.dwRGBBitCount;
(4) IDirectDraw_QueryInterface(dd, IID_IDirect3D {3BBA0080-2421-11CF-A31A-00AA00B93356}, the v1 interface avp.exe uses at 0x559599), then EnumDevices. Take the first device whose HW D3DDEVICEDESC.dcmColorModel != 0 (0x559310) and read its dwDeviceRenderBitDepth (offset 0x9c; DDBD_16=0x400, DDBD_32=0x100). If there is no such device, write nothing;
(5) bpp = 32 if (w,h,32) is enumerated and DDBD_32 is set; else 16 if (w,h,16) and DDBD_16; else none;
(6) if none: when <file> exists, has an all-zero GUID and names a W/H/BPP that is not in that filtered list, DeleteFileA it, because avp.exe 0x559810 would otherwise keep mode index -1 and read W/H/BPP from the DDCAPS tail. Print 'AvP_Video.cfg: WxH not offered - game default 640x480x16' and exit 0;
(7) else build 32 bytes: 16 x 00, le32 0, le32 w, le32 h, le32 bpp (example 1920x1080x32 = 00*16 00000000 80070000 38040000 20000000; reference encoder apply.avp_video_cfg()). If the file already holds exactly these bytes, print unchanged. Otherwise write it CREATE_ALWAYS, read it back, memcmp, and exit 1 on mismatch;
(8) keep the mingw, no-SSE, pure-Win32 build.
